  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Requires SeliseBlocks.Genesis.OS 4.3.11 or later. The release entity classes (Repo, Build, RepositoryWebhook, DependencyTrackProjects, HostingProvider, Region, MachineConfig, DeploySettings, BuildEventResponse, GithubWebhook, Config, RepoProject) now come from Genesis in Blocks.Genesis.Entities.Release; the copies in the bundled Devops.DomainService assembly are removed, so a host that used them must switch to the Genesis namespace. Stored documents keep the same collections and field names. Reads and writes of Repos, Builds and RepositoryWebhooks go through the Genesis data access resolver (row filter, projection, View column rules, Repo schema validation rules and defaults, and on insert the requester added to Read, Update and Delete UserIds); it is skipped without a signed-in user or when the call targets another tenant's database, and a refusing rule surfaces as DataValidationException. RegisterBlocksReleaseServicesAsync now calls AddBlocksDataAccess(), which is not idempotent: a host that also calls it gets the registrations twice (the last one wins; both use the default options). The Dependency-Track project mapping is kept in the Genesis key-value store under dependency-track-project:{tenantId}, falling back to the old DependencyTrackProjects collection on read, so the host must provide IKeyValueStore (ApplicationConfigurations.ConfigureServices registers it). Built-in notifications are sent for build, deployment, repo secret and GitHub events. Switching a repository between Manual and Auto now saves the GitHub webhook's active state and reports whether the switch succeeded; existing repositories are corrected on their next switch.",
